  "facts": [
    "Bennelong Bridge, spanning 330 metres across Homebush Bay, opened on 22 May 2016 after construction began on 1 September 2014, linking Rhodes and the newly designated suburb of Wentworth Point.",
    "Unlike most Sydney crossings, Bennelong Bridge is a designated T‑Way that excludes private cars, carrying only Transit Systems bus 526, Busways bus 533, Baylink Shuttle, cyclists, pedestrians, and emergency vehicles.",
    "The bridge was the first in the region funded entirely by property developers, who received increased development density at Wentworth Point in exchange for building the structure under a voluntary planning agreement."
